<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#tui-haatakalaua">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tuʻi Haʻatakalaua</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tu'i Ha'atakalaua</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tuʻi Haʻatakalaua was the second line of Tongan kings, created in the 15th century after the assassination of the Tuʻi Tonga Takalaua. His son Kauʻulufonua I avenged him and gave his brother Moʻungāmotuʻa authority over everyday government, while the Tuʻi Tonga kept sacred rank. In the 17th century a junior branch of this line, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tui-kanokupolu">Tuʻi Kanokupolu</a>, took over its executive role, and from it descends the present royal house.</p></div>
